  "caption": "A thimble in Swedish is a fingerborg: a finger castle. Borg is an old word for a castle or fortress, as in Göteborg.\n\nOther things you wear are just as literal: an earring is an örhänge (ear hanger) and a necklace is a halsband (neck band).\n\nDo you still own a thimble?",
